cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Agent Reliability Engineering Database (AREDB)"
abstract: >-
  A public registry of catastrophic autonomous-agent failures, indexed onto the
  OWASP Agentic Security Initiative Top 10. Each incident carries a stable
  ARE-YYYY-NNN identifier, a cited source, and an honest coverage flag stating
  whether the failure is deterministically preventable at the action layer.
  Cite the identifiers (e.g. ARE-2026-001) as the shared reference for the field.
message: >-
  If you use this database, please cite it and keep the ARE-YYYY-NNN
  identifiers intact. Attribution satisfies the CC-BY-4.0 license.
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "AgentX-Core"
    website: "https://agentx-core.com"
# `url` is the canonical landing page and is the field citation renderers
# actually emit (GitHub's cite widget, Zenodo, BibTeX/APA). It must point at the
# AREDB landing page, not the source repo, or every generated citation sends the
# reader to GitHub and the domain never appears. `repository-code` (NOT bare
# `repository`, which means an archival repository in CFF 1.2.0) carries the source.
url: "https://agentx-core.com/aredb"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vdalal/ARE-Incident-Database"
# KEEP IN SYNC, all three move together at release: this `version` + `date-released`,
# the CHANGELOG.md release heading, and the `v*` git tag. `date-released` is what
# supplies the year in a rendered citation; without it citations render year-less.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-11"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - agent-reliability-engineering
  - ARE
  - AI-agent-failures
  - agent-security
  - incident-taxonomy
  - OWASP-ASI
